@startuml secuencia-registro-consulta
' Flujo de registro y consulta en operación normal — Fase 2
' Renderizar con PlantUML (plugin de VS Code o plantuml.jar)

title Registro y consulta en operación normal

actor "Usuario (cliente Ubuntu)" as c
participant "Servidor 1\n(Debian, :5000)" as s1
database "db1\n(PostgreSQL)" as d1
participant "Servidor 2\n(Fedora, :5001)" as s2
database "db2\n(PostgreSQL)" as d2

== Registro de información ==

c -> s1 : POST /api/records\n{"payload": "..."}
s1 -> d1 : INSERT INTO records\n+ outbox (pendiente)
d1 --> s1 : ok

s1 -> s2 : REPLICATE {registro}\n(canal TCP :6000 -> :6001)
s2 -> d2 : UPSERT por UUID\n(ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING)
d2 --> s2 : ok
s2 --> s1 : ACK
s1 -> d1 : outbox: eliminar pendiente
d1 --> s1 : ok

s1 --> c : 201 {"served_by": "server1", "record": {...}}

== Consulta de información ==

c -> s2 : GET /api/records
s2 -> d2 : SELECT ... ORDER BY created_at DESC
d2 --> s2 : registros
s2 --> c : 200 {"served_by": "server2", "records": [...]}

note right of c : La consulta la atiende el\nServidor 2 con los mismos\ndatos: replicación activa-activa.

== Heartbeat (cada 5 s, ambos sentidos) ==

s1 -> s2 : PING (TCP)
s2 --> s1 : PONG {server_id, record_count}
s2 -> s1 : PING (TCP)
s1 --> s2 : PONG {server_id, record_count}

@enduml
